WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:03.650
Wealth, fame, power...

3
00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:04.440
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

4
00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:07.820
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates, obtained everything the world has to offer.

5
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:07.360
attained this and everything else
the world had to offer.

6
00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.820
And his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

7
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:11.660
What he said in his final moments drove countless souls to the seas.

8
00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.660
You want my treasure?

9
00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:13.700
You can have it!

10
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:15.450
Go ahead.

11
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:17.040
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

12
00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:16.660
Find it!

13
00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.250
Everything is right where I left it!

14
00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.250
Now you just have to find it!

15
00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.750
These words lured
men to the Grand Line

16
00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:26.380
People set their sights on the Grand Line in pursuit of their dreams.

17
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:26.920
in pursuit of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine!

18
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:29.630
The world has truly entered the Great Pirate Era!

19
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.850
This is the time known as
the Great Pirate Era!

20
00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:35.640
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

21
00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:41.440
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

22
00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:42.690
One Piece!

23
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:52.700
Compasses? Not for me. Left them all behind

24
00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:58.500
I'm headed out to sea, with my heart serving as guide

25
00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:04.540
Following the ancient map to the spot marked "X" reveals

26
00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:09.760
Yeah, it's only legendary till someone proves it's real

27
00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.710
When the world's got you down,

28
00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:16.850
lean on your crew, they'll turn it around

29
00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:22.190
Their biorhythm will carry you through

30
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.230
We're gonna make the most of it

31
00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:31.400
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

32
00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:36.990
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

33
00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:40.040
Got some change to my name,

34
00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:43.250
and maybe you wanna be my friend?

35
00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:48.130
We are, we are on the cruise!

36
00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:49.760
WE ARE!

37
00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:54.680
<b>You're the Weird Animal</b>

38
00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:06.270
You pathetic, little maggots.

39
00:02:06.970 --> 00:02:09.360
You would knowingly
attack the invincible fleet

40
00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:12.980
of pirates commanded by
Captain Usopp of the Going Merry?!

41
00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:18.330
Ah! Attack them! Show no mercy!

42
00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:25.290
Geez. I really
expected you guys

43
00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:26.920
to be a little bit
more lively than this.

44
00:02:27.070 --> 00:02:28.500
– I'm finished!

45
00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:31.440
Heh, heh. Look! Our pirate mark!

46
00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:34.940
Now that Usopp's joined, we got four people,
that's almost a whole crew!

47
00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:37.050
I think it's about time
we got our own flag!

48
00:02:37.270 --> 00:02:39.310
Uh... Luffy?

49
00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:41.020
Is that really gonna be our mark?

50
00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:43.980
Heh. Whaddya think? Nice, huh?

51
00:02:44.150 --> 00:02:46.020
Our mark should be scary.

52
00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:48.020
It should strike fear
into our enemies' hearts.

53
00:02:48.190 --> 00:02:51.860
If our enemies were terrified infants,
then this would be perfect.

54
00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:55.490
You guys really should've
told me about this.

55
00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:59.030
Maybe you didn't know this about me,
but I am an artist.

56
00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:00.790
Does that mean you can draw?

57
00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:03.700
Heh. When it comes to painting,
I'm in a league of my own!

58
00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:07.210
I've been drawing graffiti
for fifty years straight.

59
00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:12.920
Behold! A priceless work of pirate art!

60
00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:13.940
Ta-dah!

61
00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:16.510
Looks a lot like you
on that flag. Jerk!

62
00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:22.010
So, how do you like this one?

63
00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:24.140
Wow. That's actually
pretty good, Usopp.

64
00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:26.140
Yeah! Keep it! That's the one!

65
00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:29.400
So, we've finally settled on it.
This is gonna be our mark?

66
00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:30.600
Sure is!

67
00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:32.690
Hey, Usopp! Draw one on the sail, too!

68
00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:33.650
Right!

69
00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:38.740
Okay! It's all done.

70
00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:43.540
Now the Going Merry has everything
she could possibly need!

71
00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:47.830
Ah... I'm pooped.

72
00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:52.590
Huh?

73
00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:56.380
Are we going the right way?
Seems kinda dangerous.

74
00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:57.470
What's that?!

75
00:03:57.470 --> 00:03:58.370
Hold on.

76
00:03:58.370 --> 00:04:00.550
Hm?

77
00:04:00.570 --> 00:04:02.600
That's the place.

78
00:04:02.710 --> 00:04:04.420
Yep. There's no doubt about it.

79
00:04:04.420 --> 00:04:07.060
Hey, what do ya see out there?
Is it something cool?

80
00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:09.730
The legendary Treasure Island.

81
00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:11.530
You mean the Treasure Island?

82
00:04:11.530 --> 00:04:13.070
Even I've heard of that place.

83
00:04:13.130 --> 00:04:15.600
Yeah. I'm not surprised,
this place is famous

84
00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:18.570
the world over. And so are
the crazy stories about it.

85
00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:20.490
What crazy stories?

86
00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:22.610
Legend has it that
whoever's dumb enough

87
00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:25.950
to sail close to the island
incurs a god's wrath.

88
00:04:30.170 --> 00:04:32.750
Now we know that all those
stories were true, guys!

89
00:04:32.770 --> 00:04:34.210
This is a god's wrath!

90
00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:35.880
I think that sounds pretty cool.

91
00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:39.510
– Hey, wait! We're not gonna...
– You bet we are!

92
00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:46.770
Let's go to Treasure Island!

93
00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:48.680
This is gonna be bad!

94
00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:32.440
I'm tired.

95
00:05:32.450 --> 00:05:33.940
Nap time.

96
00:05:35.690 --> 00:05:38.650
How can he possibly sleep
in such a creepy place?

97
00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:40.950
He's either dumb,
or he's got nerves of steel.

98
00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:50.910
What's happening?! Are we in danger?!

99
00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:52.080
Uh... What?!

100
00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:54.750
No, I was just making up
a little dance to liven things up!

101
00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:02.220
Hey. Come on, stop that, Luffy.

102
00:06:11.150 --> 00:06:12.690
What's going on?!

103
00:06:15.790 --> 00:06:18.760
Leave now!

104
00:06:18.760 --> 00:06:21.730
– Who's there?!
– Leave now!

105
00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:24.400
Guys? Where's that voice coming from?

106
00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:27.490
I am
the vengeful island god!

107
00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:30.830
Leave at once if you value your lives!

108
00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:31.950
Island god?

109
00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:34.670
Wait.
You guys are pirates, right?

110
00:06:34.670 --> 00:06:35.400
Well, yeah.

111
00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:37.570
Ah... I knew it.

112
00:06:37.570 --> 00:06:40.550
Why would a god need
to ask something like that?

113
00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:43.930
I dunno. I-I mean,
take one more step into the forest!

114
00:06:43.930 --> 00:06:46.010
The instant you do,
you will instantly receive

115
00:06:46.030 --> 00:06:50.640
my divine punishment and meet your doom,
which is my punishment. Wait, uh.

116
00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:52.870
Okay. That made no sense at all.

117
00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:54.020
This guy is weird.

118
00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:55.870
Yeah. What's his deal, anyway?

119
00:06:55.870 --> 00:06:58.900
What did
you say, straw hat boy?!

120
00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:06.540
What are these things?

121
00:07:06.540 --> 00:07:08.320
They used to be humans!

122
00:07:08.340 --> 00:07:12.830
They came looking for treasure,
but all they found was my wrath!

123
00:07:13.220 --> 00:07:16.550
Uh. You transformed them?!
Then you are a god!

124
00:07:16.550 --> 00:07:19.310
Look at all these weird things!

125
00:07:19.310 --> 00:07:20.830
Huh. So, is this a pig?

126
00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:22.920
Could be a lion.

127
00:07:26.630 --> 00:07:29.470
You stretchy
freak of nature! What are you?!

128
00:07:29.470 --> 00:07:32.720
One time I ate a devil fruit.
So now I'm a rubber person.

129
00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:35.040
Yeah, right.
A devil fruit?

130
00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:38.020
I heard those same stupid stories
back when I was a pirate, but...

131
00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:39.770
Back when you were a pirate?

132
00:07:39.990 --> 00:07:41.980
I mean, uh...
No! I wasn't reminiscing

133
00:07:41.990 --> 00:07:44.650
about the old days!
Enough of that kinda talk!

134
00:07:44.670 --> 00:07:46.100
I don't wanna hear about
the old days! Got it?!

135
00:07:46.100 --> 00:07:48.570
Are you nuts? You're the one
who brought it up.

136
00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:50.950
You faker! You sound
too dumb to be a god!

137
00:07:51.040 --> 00:07:54.660
Shut up! If you won't leave,
then prepare for my divine judgment!

138
00:08:03.380 --> 00:08:05.550
You're really pushing
your luck... "god."

139
00:08:05.550 --> 00:08:07.170
How are you not dead?!

140
00:08:07.410 --> 00:08:09.420
– There you are.
– Don't move!

141
00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:11.350
I said don't move!

142
00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:17.850
No! That can't be!

143
00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:19.060
Hey, "island god."

144
00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:21.790
Even mortals know
bullets can't hurt a rubber man!

145
00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:23.820
Maybe not, but I still hate them.

146
00:08:23.930 --> 00:08:26.570
You're
some kind of monster!

147
00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:27.780
Over there!

148
00:08:28.470 --> 00:08:30.870
Hey, look. Found his gun.

149
00:08:35.490 --> 00:08:36.870
Where did he go?

150
00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:40.620
Huh?!

151
00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:42.770
What is this?

152
00:08:42.770 --> 00:08:45.250
Could it be the island god?

153
00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:47.760
It's moving!

154
00:08:57.510 --> 00:08:58.230
Stand me up!

155
00:08:58.990 --> 00:09:00.310
Stand me up already!

156
00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:01.390
It's a person!

157
00:09:01.390 --> 00:09:03.860
Awesome! He's like
a talking scrub brush!

158
00:09:03.990 --> 00:09:06.650
That's it? You're not
even a minor deity.

159
00:09:06.660 --> 00:09:07.940
You're more like a box.

160
00:09:08.260 --> 00:09:10.490
Come on! Stand me up now!

161
00:09:10.530 --> 00:09:12.490
Relax. Here.

162
00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:16.950
There. You're all set now.

163
00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:20.660
<b>Gaimon
Inhabitant of the Island</b>

164
00:09:21.340 --> 00:09:24.130
You're a pretty
popular guy, Mr. Island God.

165
00:09:24.170 --> 00:09:27.630
So lemme get this straight, these crazy
animals helped you scare off the pirates

166
00:09:27.640 --> 00:09:29.470
who came to this place
looking for treasure?

167
00:09:29.650 --> 00:09:33.010
I've never seen a person stuffed
inside a treasure chest before.

168
00:09:33.390 --> 00:09:35.260
You're a real-life "jack-in-the-box."

169
00:09:35.490 --> 00:09:40.430
Yes. Ironically, I am in fact
in a box, and my name is... You idiot!

170
00:09:40.560 --> 00:09:43.260
I'm a person! Not a toy!

171
00:09:43.260 --> 00:09:45.260
I've been stranded,
alone, on this island,

172
00:09:45.260 --> 00:09:48.110
and stuck in this contemptible box
for twenty years.

173
00:09:48.530 --> 00:09:49.820
That long?

174
00:09:57.560 --> 00:10:00.660
So you've been all alone on this island
for twenty years? Amazing.

175
00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:04.630
Yeah, just take a look at me.
I got a beard like a wild man.

176
00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:07.340
And in all that time,
you're the first people

177
00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:09.540
that I've had a real conversation with.

178
00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:11.050
Can you understand how painful that is?

179
00:10:11.980 --> 00:10:13.010
That's ridiculous.

180
00:10:13.010 --> 00:10:14.220
What did you say?!

181
00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:17.250
Oh, oh... here you are.

182
00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:19.140
I've been looking
all over for you guys.

183
00:10:19.150 --> 00:10:22.230
How could you have slept through
everything that's just happened?

184
00:10:31.990 --> 00:10:33.490
What the heck is that?!

185
00:10:33.690 --> 00:10:35.110
He finally sees him.

186
00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:37.190
Check it out! He's in a treasure chest.

187
00:10:37.190 --> 00:10:39.450
Like a "jack-in-the-box." But real!

188
00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:44.290
Yes. Ironically, I am in fact
in a box, and my name is... You idiot!

189
00:10:44.300 --> 00:10:46.290
We've already been through all that!

190
00:10:46.300 --> 00:10:47.590
Zoro! Gimme a hand!

191
00:10:48.680 --> 00:10:52.720
Oww! What are you doing?!
Stop it, would you?!

192
00:10:52.720 --> 00:10:53.840
You're pulling my head off! Stop it!

193
00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:56.260
Sorry, I'm afraid you're stuck.

194
00:10:56.290 --> 00:10:57.340
Don't be stupid!

195
00:10:57.360 --> 00:11:01.090
I've been stuck inside this blasted
treasure chest for so many years now

196
00:11:01.090 --> 00:11:03.600
that it's slowly become
a part of my body!

197
00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:06.060
If you try to break it,
you'll break my body, too!

198
00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:08.190
You're a strange little man.

199
00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:11.820
Alright, guys,
enough about me, who are you?

200
00:11:11.870 --> 00:11:15.360
You're not like any of those other pirates
who've come around here, that's for sure.

201
00:11:16.610 --> 00:11:17.440
I'm Luffy!

202
00:11:17.440 --> 00:11:19.070
I'm gonna get the One Piece.

203
00:11:19.070 --> 00:11:21.120
And then I'm gonna be
King of the Pirates.

204
00:11:21.270 --> 00:11:23.540
The One Piece?!
Don't tell me you idiots

205
00:11:23.540 --> 00:11:26.280
are actually planning
to sail on the Grand Line!

206
00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:28.130
Yup! We got a chart right here.

207
00:11:28.710 --> 00:11:30.250
Don't be such a fool!

208
00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:32.280
The Grand Line's a graveyard!

209
00:11:32.280 --> 00:11:34.670
I once saw a group of pirates
who had managed to escape

210
00:11:34.690 --> 00:11:37.290
from that horrible place,
and I'll never forget it.

211
00:11:37.290 --> 00:11:40.460
It was an awful sight.
They were just the hollow shells

212
00:11:40.460 --> 00:11:43.010
of the men that they used to be.
There's no telling

213
00:11:43.010 --> 00:11:46.010
what horrors they witnessed
in that ghastly place.

214
00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:48.880
Not one among them even tried to speak.

215
00:11:48.880 --> 00:11:49.730
Mm...

216
00:11:49.750 --> 00:11:52.070
Now listen to me well, young pirates.

217
00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:54.990
The rumors of the One Piece
spawn more rumors.

218
00:11:55.010 --> 00:11:55.860
Who knows what's true?

219
00:11:56.410 --> 00:11:58.360
It's been only twenty-odd
years since the start

220
00:11:58.380 --> 00:12:01.030
of the Great Pirate Era,
and the One Piece is already

221
00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:03.830
a dream within a dream beyond a legend!

222
00:12:06.490 --> 00:12:08.750
So, which one of these
is the Grand Line?

223
00:12:08.760 --> 00:12:12.000
I dunno. Figured you could tell me,
Mr. Scrub Brush Guy.

224
00:12:12.020 --> 00:12:14.190
Sorry, I never learned
how to read a sea chart.

225
00:12:14.190 --> 00:12:15.710
I never did, either.

226
00:12:17.300 --> 00:12:19.930
Ignorance is bliss, isn't it?

227
00:12:20.030 --> 00:12:23.080
Anyway, even if we do somehow
make it to the Grand Line,

228
00:12:23.080 --> 00:12:26.850
the best idea would be to get
as much treasure as we can and then escape.

229
00:12:27.070 --> 00:12:29.810
You go ahead and do that,
I'm gonna find the One Piece.

230
00:12:29.920 --> 00:12:32.300
Where do you get
all that confidence of yours?

231
00:12:32.300 --> 00:12:34.230
I'll get it! You'll see.

232
00:12:34.230 --> 00:12:37.190
Whatever you say.

233
00:12:39.060 --> 00:12:40.390
You're me.

234
00:12:40.390 --> 00:12:41.400
Hm?

235
00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:44.030
You're exactly like me.
You even look like me.

236
00:12:44.040 --> 00:12:45.400
We could be twins.

237
00:12:45.400 --> 00:12:47.410
How can you say he looks like you?

238
00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:50.860
Young man. I understand about
the pursuit of your dreams!

239
00:12:50.860 --> 00:12:53.840
When I was a younger man,
we used to feel the same way!

240
00:12:54.370 --> 00:12:55.670
What do you mean, "we"?

241
00:12:55.690 --> 00:12:58.920
We were willing to put our lives on the line
to search for treasure.

242
00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:02.710
It was that single-minded zeal
that changed the course of my life forever.

243
00:13:02.710 --> 00:13:03.980
Wait. Slow down.
What are you talking about?

244
00:13:03.980 --> 00:13:07.560
It happened twenty years ago...
I was a much younger man then.

245
00:13:07.710 --> 00:13:10.810
My fellow pirates and I
landed on this island with a single purpose.

246
00:13:12.240 --> 00:13:15.730
To find the treasure
that was said to rest here.

247
00:13:18.820 --> 00:13:23.220
Two hundred men have searched for
an entire month, and nothing has been found!

248
00:13:23.220 --> 00:13:26.480
The only treasure chest
we've uncovered is empty!

249
00:13:26.480 --> 00:13:28.500
Pack up, men! We're leaving.

250
00:13:32.050 --> 00:13:34.570
What are you
looking at, Gaimon? It's time to go!

251
00:13:34.570 --> 00:13:36.000
Right.

252
00:13:34.880 --> 00:13:36.960
<b>Gaimon
(Twenty Years Ago)</b>

253
00:13:38.270 --> 00:13:40.280
Did anyone look way up there?

254
00:13:40.280 --> 00:13:44.260
I know that the captain stayed
down here the whole month.

255
00:13:46.930 --> 00:13:49.600
I'd better go ahead
and double-check.

256
00:13:55.300 --> 00:13:58.000
I couldn't believe my own eyes!

257
00:13:58.000 --> 00:14:01.070
Ha! I found it. Guys, it's up here!

258
00:14:01.070 --> 00:14:03.410
Hey! You guy...

259
00:14:13.480 --> 00:14:16.380
That's when
I got stuck in this chest!

260
00:14:17.590 --> 00:14:21.380
When I came to, my crew
was already far out to sea.

261
00:14:25.390 --> 00:14:30.260
Hold on. Yes. I believe this means that
the entire fortune belongs to me now!

262
00:14:30.260 --> 00:14:37.310
I can't climb up like this!
I can't get out! I can't get out!

263
00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:42.940
Hey! Come back! Come back, please!

264
00:14:42.940 --> 00:14:46.480
And after all this time,
the fortune I found but only saw

265
00:14:46.480 --> 00:14:49.910
for an instant has never strayed
far from my lonely old mind.

266
00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:53.400
Pirates have come here countless times
to search for my treasure.

267
00:14:53.400 --> 00:14:56.670
But fortunately, my friends here
help me scare them away.

268
00:14:56.770 --> 00:15:02.010
That's how I've kept my treasure
safe and sound for the past twenty years.

269
00:15:02.570 --> 00:15:03.920
It's my treasure!

270
00:15:04.620 --> 00:15:07.140
No question. It's yours, all right!

271
00:15:07.270 --> 00:15:08.970
You know, I think we can help you out.

272
00:15:09.080 --> 00:15:12.350
Gaimon, why don't we get
the treasure down for you?

273
00:15:12.420 --> 00:15:14.560
Wait, do you mean it?

274
00:15:14.020 --> 00:15:14.560
Yeah.

275
00:15:15.320 --> 00:15:16.480
Nami.

276
00:15:16.490 --> 00:15:19.110
Hey, aren't you a thief
that only steals from pirates?

277
00:15:19.390 --> 00:15:20.270
How rude!

278
00:15:21.390 --> 00:15:23.280
I am a thief, but I have a conscience!

279
00:15:47.200 --> 00:15:47.930
It's here?

280
00:15:47.940 --> 00:15:51.680
Yes, this is the place.
It's all up there.

281
00:15:55.610 --> 00:15:57.620
The time has finally come!

282
00:15:57.620 --> 00:15:58.940
It's a great day!

283
00:15:59.350 --> 00:16:00.440
Get to it, Straw Hat!

284
00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:02.520
Sure thing! Gum-Gum...

285
00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:09.280
...Rocket!

286
00:16:12.530 --> 00:16:14.370
Awesome!

287
00:16:17.940 --> 00:16:20.130
Hey! The chests! You see?!

288
00:16:25.510 --> 00:16:27.910
I found 'em! Six treasure chests!

289
00:16:27.910 --> 00:16:31.850
Yes! Good work!

290
00:16:31.850 --> 00:16:35.750
Now it's mine! I got my treasure!
C'mon, toss it down,

291
00:16:35.750 --> 00:16:38.770
I wanna see it! Go ahead
and toss it down, boy!

292
00:16:38.790 --> 00:16:40.790
Let's have a look at it!

293
00:16:40.790 --> 00:16:41.690
No way!

294
00:16:41.760 --> 00:16:42.980
No way?!

295
00:16:43.960 --> 00:16:46.860
I don't wanna. Sucks for you!

296
00:16:46.860 --> 00:16:50.360
What kind of crap is that, Luffy?
Give the man his gold!

297
00:16:55.560 --> 00:16:57.730
Hey, I'm not joking around, mister!

298
00:16:57.730 --> 00:16:58.790
It doesn't matter.

299
00:16:59.970 --> 00:17:01.070
It's all right.

300
00:17:01.070 --> 00:17:02.070
It's not all right.

301
00:17:02.070 --> 00:17:04.460
Gaimon. You've been
guarding that treasure

302
00:17:04.470 --> 00:17:06.420
with your heart and soul
for the past twenty years!

303
00:17:07.810 --> 00:17:10.510
Straw Hat.

304
00:17:10.510 --> 00:17:12.390
You're a great guy!

305
00:17:12.450 --> 00:17:14.600
Uh. What do you mean he's great?

306
00:17:15.150 --> 00:17:19.770
I always had an inkling that...
this might be the case.

307
00:17:19.850 --> 00:17:22.940
I tried not to think
about it. But still...

308
00:17:24.120 --> 00:17:26.320
They're empty!

309
00:17:27.830 --> 00:17:31.370
Yep. Every last one of 'em.

310
00:17:31.370 --> 00:17:36.910
How sad. The treasure he guarded for twenty
long years was just a bunch of empty boxes.

311
00:17:36.910 --> 00:17:41.710
It happens all the time with
treasures that have maps leading to them.

312
00:17:41.810 --> 00:17:45.170
You set out on a quest to find it,
but someone else got to it first.

313
00:17:45.940 --> 00:17:48.920
That's the kind of risk you have to take
when you're a treasure-hunting pirate.

314
00:17:49.740 --> 00:17:53.760
You can waste a whole lifetime
searching and never once touch treasure.

315
00:17:53.880 --> 00:17:56.180
Plenty of pirates lived
like that. Believe me!

316
00:17:56.410 --> 00:18:01.080
Try not to
be too upset, old man!

317
00:18:01.080 --> 00:18:03.650
It's a good thing we came along
after twenty years!

318
00:18:04.050 --> 00:18:06.940
Thirty years later, and
you might've been dead!

319
00:18:07.930 --> 00:18:09.320
Oh, Straw Hat...

320
00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:11.320
– Luffy...
– Is he...?

321
00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:13.860
Since this treasure hunt's a bust,
you're gonna need

322
00:18:13.870 --> 00:18:15.620
something else to fill your time.

323
00:18:15.640 --> 00:18:18.410
Why don't you join up with us
and search for the One Piece?

324
00:18:18.610 --> 00:18:22.080
What? Really? You're asking me?

325
00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:25.380
Oh... I know how I must look to you.

326
00:18:25.510 --> 00:18:28.380
Other people wouldn't even
speak to me, but you were kind!

327
00:18:29.950 --> 00:18:38.460
It's been so many years since
I've had a friend!

328
00:18:38.460 --> 00:18:40.680
Thank you!

329
00:18:50.520 --> 00:18:54.820
Are you sure you wanna
stay on the island, Gaimon?

330
00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:57.900
Yes, I'm sure. There's something
here far more valuable

331
00:18:57.900 --> 00:18:59.950
than treasure that
I feel I must protect.

332
00:18:59.950 --> 00:19:00.880
Huh?

333
00:19:00.880 --> 00:19:02.620
Worth more than gold?

334
00:19:04.420 --> 00:19:08.590
For the past twenty years, these guys have
stood by my side through thick and thin.

335
00:19:09.610 --> 00:19:10.840
I can't leave 'em.

336
00:19:17.740 --> 00:19:19.510
Now that I know
there's no treasure here,

337
00:19:20.160 --> 00:19:23.180
I somehow finally feel free.
Without that heavy burden,

338
00:19:23.340 --> 00:19:26.180
I can concentrate on the things
that really matter to me.

339
00:19:26.180 --> 00:19:29.520
And besides, after all these years,
I've grown fond of this little box.

340
00:19:29.880 --> 00:19:33.180
Too bad! You're a neat guy.
Pretty cool for a scrub brush.

341
00:19:33.180 --> 00:19:35.490
The weird creatures here
are your true friends.

342
00:19:35.490 --> 00:19:38.280
Yep! And he's
the weirdest of them all.

343
00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:39.450
Excuse me!

344
00:19:48.840 --> 00:19:52.550
See ya! Take care, okay?!

345
00:19:52.550 --> 00:19:54.510
Bye, Gaimon!

346
00:19:56.890 --> 00:19:58.660
Straw Hat guy.

347
00:19:58.660 --> 00:20:02.000
Don't ever give up on making
all your dreams come true.

348
00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:05.350
If the legendary One Piece
exists out there...

349
00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:08.190
then it's yours.
I hope it finds you well.

350
00:20:09.930 --> 00:20:15.900
And when you have it, buy the world!

351
00:20:22.120 --> 00:20:28.980
As a kid I had a dream of a dazzling treasure

352
00:20:29.180 --> 00:20:36.000
I had a map in my head that I knew would lead me

353
00:20:36.250 --> 00:20:43.100
Charted a course all on my own so nobody would beat me

354
00:20:43.220 --> 00:20:50.360
The promised land was in my hand drew a line in the sand

355
00:20:53.060 --> 00:20:55.740
Look where I am

356
00:20:57.970 --> 00:21:04.150
My one ambitions slipping right through my hands

357
00:21:04.490 --> 00:21:11.420
But if the world ever changes Ill call out your name

358
00:21:11.580 --> 00:21:18.500
We could return to a time when our lives were still the same

359
00:21:18.630 --> 00:21:25.630
Take me to the place where memories remain

360
00:21:25.730 --> 00:21:31.500
Please dont ever let them fade
